From 3336180ecb205a8651cdf2c298c63fe076819ae5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:02:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] In-game settings menu (F2) and a live settings registry

The launcher's options (ga2_options.h, one table shared with the launcher) become runtime-adjustable
values (ga2_settings): the engines take them from the environment as before (or settings.ini under
GA2_DATA_DIR for what is unset), and the in-game menu changes them and saves settings.ini at once,
so launcher and game stay in sync. F2 opens the settings page of the cheat menu (the cheats page has
a Settings row for gamepad and VR controllers).

Live: display, screen shape (window follows), sides, 2D scene size, 2D filter (shaders built on demand),
dithering (applied at vsync), button prompts, on-screen pad, texture dump (textures loaded from then
on), frame rate between 60 and the run's top rate (governor ladder follows setUserCap). Hor+ is live
through the game side (SC native/compat). Language, resolution, VR and frame rates above the run's top
are marked restart and applied by the next start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
